Vella is a native Swift application. Speech recognition runs on MLX through
mlx-swift in sandboxed helper processes; no Python runs at runtime. Third-party
code in the app is listed, with each licence text, in THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md
(shipped in Vella.app/Contents/Resources next to this file).

Speech models
-------------
Worker/Sources/MLXAudioSTT is adapted from mlx-audio-swift
(https://github.com/Blaizzy/mlx-audio-swift, revision
01dec7c9bdce3088a6b6b7ab9f2e403458195efb, MIT, Copyright 2025 Prince Canuma),
changed for Vella: local loading only, and optimized paths behind a load-time
self-test. The Parakeet front end and the streaming DSP follow mlx-audio 0.5.1
(MIT, Copyright 2024 Prince Canuma); the Whisper decoding settings follow
mlx-whisper (MIT, Copyright 2023 Apple Inc.).

Models
------
Vella bundles no model weights. When the user confirms a download, it fetches
them from Hugging Face; each keeps its own licence (Resources/models.json and
THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md list them).

Audio
-----
The self-test and calibration clips are from LibriSpeech (Panayotov, Chen,
Povey and Khudanpur; https://www.openslr.org/12/), with LibriSpeech-PC text
(Meister et al., NVIDIA; https://www.openslr.org/145/), under CC BY 4.0.

